# Reset a forgotten Microsoft account password

Applies To

Microsoft account Microsoft account dashboard

![](/images/copilot-banner-logo.svg?v=c7N671DRofjY-cWMgpLqYectYsldAQJt4-EhpaQ1ZqU)

Get help with Copilot

[How do I verify identity for Microsoft account recovery?](https://m365.cloud.microsoft/chat/entity1-d870f6cd-4aa5-4d42-9626-?fromcode=cmmk8w6ik52&cmmid=cmmk8w6ik52&ocid=cmmk8w6ik52)
[What if I can't change or reset local account password?](https://m365.cloud.microsoft/chat/entity1-d870f6cd-4aa5-4d42-9626-?fromcode=cmmk8w6ik52&cmmid=cmmk8w6ik52&ocid=cmmk8w6ik52)
[Can I get a Microsoft account verification code?](https://m365.cloud.microsoft/chat/entity1-d870f6cd-4aa5-4d42-9626-?fromcode=cmmk8w6ik52&cmmid=cmmk8w6ik52&ocid=cmmk8w6ik52)

Note

* If you know your password but just want to change it, go to [account.microsoft.com/security](https://account.microsoft.com/security) and select [Change password](https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?linkid=2274069).
* If you know your username and password but they have stopped working, read [My username and password have stopped working](my-username-and-password-have-stopped-working).

### Step 1: Select 'Forgot password?' on the Microsoft account sign-in page

If the "Enter password" window is still open select **Forgotten your password?**

If not, select Reset password below, enter the username name for the account you're trying to reset, and select **Next**.

[Reset password](https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?linkid=2273955)

![Forgot Password image](../media/forgotpassword.png)

### Step 2: Verify your identity for Microsoft account recovery

For your protection, Microsoft must verify your identity before you can proceed with resetting your password.

1. Choose how you want to receive a verification code.

![Verify ID2 image](../media/verify-id.png)

Important

* If you don't see an option for where to send a code, or you no longer have access to any of the verification options shown, use this [sign-in helper tool](https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?linkid=2242650).
* If you don't recognize any of the verification email or phone options, use this [sign-in helper tool](https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?linkid=2241144).

2. Select **Next**.

### Step 3: Get a Microsoft account verification code

For your protection, we will ask you to confirm the verification details you select. If you cannot get a code, read [Troubleshooting verification code issues](troubleshoot-microsoft-verification-code-issues).

1. Retype the first part of the email address or the last four digits of the phone number hinted at in the previous window.
2. Select **Get code**.
3. Microsoft will send a verification code to the email or phone number you selected.
4. Go to the recovery phone or email for where you expect to receive the code.

![Verify ID image](../media/verify-id2.png)

### Step 4: Enter the verification code and reset your Microsoft account password

Confirm the code to create a new password. Learn [how to create a strong password](/en-us/topic/f67e4ddd-0dbe-cd75-cebe-0cfda3cf7386).

1. Paste or type the code you received and select **Next**.
2. Type your new password and select **Next**.

## See also

If these steps didn't work, or you have other account sign in issues, use our [Sign-in helper tool](https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?linkid=2214157).

[Microsoft account security info & verification codes](microsoft-account-security-info-verification-codes)

